  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1)\nScattered storms will increase in coverage this afternoon ahead of a\ncold front. SBCAPE values near 2000 J/kg will support some tall\nupdrafts that may produce some strong to damaging wind gusts.\nAdditionally, freezing levels near 11,000 ft will allow for at least\nsome small hail to develop in several of these storms. Marginally \nsevere hail near 1\" certainly possible with the tallest storms, but \nthat threat will be more limited. The severe threat will gradually \ntaper from west to east this evening, ending by 7-8 PM for our CWA.\n\nNote that these storms will be capable of brief heavy downpours as\nwell. However, the environment is such that storm motion will be more\nprogressive, which will help limit some of the hydro concerns.\nHowever, if a location where to receive multiple rounds of heavy\ndownpours or had some brief backbuilding, minor flooding issues may\nensue.",
